FUN_00414016 (GTE rotate fragment): matrix elements are SIGN-EXTENDED 16-BIT reads

The rotate fragment reads the 3x3 rotation matrix @0x74c6f0 element-wise via
`movsx eax, WORD PTR [ebp+N]` (asm 0x41401b..0x41408f) — 16-bit sign-extended shorts.
The C used the int-typed dword aliases ((int)__globmat, (int)_DAT_0074c6f6, ...) which
read TWO matrix shorts combined (identity matrix -> 0x1000_0000 = 268M element values ->
astronomic rotated vectors: live wheel z 0xf617a19d with identity matrix + sane inputs).
The dword aliases stay int elsewhere (MulMatrix's 4-byte matrix copies legitimately use
them); only this fragment's nine element reads get (short) casts, matching movsx exactly.

